course: dictionary
lesson: 7474
title: Words from castles
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name things we rarely see today, so you may not know them. Context clues help. In «the spiky portcullis», the word spiky tells you it has sharp points, and the castle setting tells you it is part of a gate.
explain: Try your idea in the sentence. A portcullis is a heavy grid of iron or wooden bars that slides down in grooves to close a castle gateway. Does "a heavy gate that drops down" fit the sentence? Yes, so your meaning works.
explain: Look at the other clues in the castle scene: «the hollow-sounding drawbridge», «men-at-arms in casquet and corselet of steel» (helmets and armour), and «mastiffs» (big guard-dogs). Every clue points to a castle that was guarded and ready for attack.
fact: A portcullis is a heavy grid of iron or wooden bars.
fact: It slides down in grooves to close a castle gateway.
fact: It was dropped to stop attackers from getting in.
fact: «Murder holes» were openings above the gateway, in medieval castles.
fact: The portcullis is also a symbol of the UK Parliament.
exercise: «The castle had a spiky portcullis.» What is a portcullis? | *A heavy grid of bars that slides down to close a gateway | A big guard-dog | A soldier's metal helmet | A long wooden bridge over a river
exercise: Why was the portcullis dropped in a castle? | To give the mastiffs a place to sleep | To let visitors in for tea | To show the castle was brand new | *To stop attackers getting in
exercise: What does «mastiffs» mean in the castle scene? | Stone walls | *Big guard-dogs | Armoured knights | Wooden bridges
test: Which is a symbol of the UK Parliament? | Oak tree | *Portcullis | Crown jewels | Red double-decker bus
test: Where were murder holes found in a medieval castle? | Inside the cellar | On the roof of the chapel | Under the moat | *Above the gateway
exam: In «the hollow-sounding drawbridge» and «the spiky portcullis», what do the clues suggest about the castle? | It was built as a place for a sleepy party | It was a shop for selling pasties | *It was built to keep enemies out | It had no gates at all
